X:8
T:Pray Goody. Dal.008
B:R.Dalton MS, 1841, Sheffield
Z:Village Music Project 2019 Rob Lands
M:C
L:1/8
Q:1/4=100
N:There is an English Ballad of this name (1802 -1819) form the Opera "Midas"
N:The opera was written by Kane O'Hara ~1760 and performed at Covent Garden.
N:https://digital.nls.uk/english-ballads/archive/74895700?mode=transcription
N:Similar music for the harp can be found here
N:https://imslp.org/wiki/File:PMLP741475-dussek-Pray_goody_-the_favorite_air_from_the_opera_of_Midas.pdf
N:The high A in the Ad Lib may not be correct. The stave has not been extended in the MS
N:but the note is clearly above the level of the G
K:G
