X:9
T:Gypsying. Dal.009
T:In The Days When We Went Gypsying,aka. Dal.009
B:R.Dalton MS, 1841, Sheffield
Z:Village Music Project 2019 Rob Lands
M:6/8
L:1/8
Q:1/4=150
N:No time signature in Manuscript
N:The song, in the key of C major and time signature 2/4, is attributed to Nathan James Sporle 1812-1853 ~1830
N:A piano arrangmenent MS of the song can be found in the Library of Congress.
N:other references Roud.1245 and Lawrence Leadley, Fiddler of Helpeston, Vol.2, No.23 also C 2/4
N:https://www.loc.gov/resource/sm1839.370030.0/?sp=1&st=list
N:The first note in the MS is a crochet, shortned to a quaver to match the tune.
K:G
